A||||5||Doni Hagan||LIGHTED WINDOW SWITCHES READY TO INSTALL!||||1||
Z||000000||Doni Hagan||11-19-2001||01:44 AM||||Well, after meeting with Bill Osmer and checking out which wires were which on the switches I grabbed a couple of weeks ago, I've spent my minimal downtime working on the installation. <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SWITCH1.jpg">  <P>Bill's article in Ogre's Cave dealt with a car w/o power mirrors. The mirror switch greatly limits the room under the plate but, as you can see, there are ways around that. Also, the switches I got (though the right ones for the mod) had different coloured wiring from the ones Bill used. <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SWITCH3.jpg">  <P>Ignore the elec tape. It's just there until the "plastiweld" dries. <P>BTW, I still have a pair of switches left and will supply a schematic and instructions with them. $20 + $4.50 shipping insured (in the US / $7.50 in Canada.) E-mail me if interested. <p>[This message has been edited by Doni Hagan (edited 11-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||dennis_6||11-19-2001||01:48 AM||||Very cool.  Unfortunely this is all going to be used as evidence.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Doni Hagan||11-19-2001||01:51 AM||||I thought my "peeps" paid you off already!<P>"Ice Pick Charlie" will be paying you a social call shortly. Look out for a black Lincoln Town Car with limo tint.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Nashco||11-19-2001||03:07 AM||||So what did you differently with the power mirror setup?  Did you just omit the wire clips and make your own stuff soldered on?  I'm having a hard time seeing any details with the pics, sorry.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||Doni Hagan||11-19-2001||11:04 PM||||Sorry...I bought the cheapest digital camera I could find. Yeah, I had to remove the wire clips entirely and weld the wiring to the tabs themselves. Also, I bypassed the need to fabricate new mounts for it and "plastiwelded" the new switches to the plate. I have a spare one if I want to re-install the stock switches. Finally, I haven't been in the car to test fit it but I thing I'm gonna have to trim the plastic frame the plate mounts to for additional clearance for the wiring. I'll post pics once I back to the car itself.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Doni Hagan||11-20-2001||06:05 PM||||Okay, I didn't have to trim the frame as expected to get them to fit. I did uncover a couple of other issues, however. This is gonna be wordy so bear with me. <P>The window motors are the same motor on both sides, just mounted differently. So when you remove the stock switches you'll note that the wiring is mirrored on both sides. I can post a diagram of the way the wires match up with each other. Also, I wanted the switches to dim with the dash lights. So rather than slave into the ashtray lights like Bill did, I opted to tap into the gear selector wiring. Once I got the wiring puzzle sussed out, the whole system works like stock! I'll post a pic as soon as I get to where my camera is. <P>||||reg||14
